{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3j2v4rrAZp86Sk6oiH3","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't commit January because the file has a bad row.\n\n**The bad row (line 33):**\n```\nR2601-032,C117,399.31,wholesale\n```\nIt has 4 fields where the header has 5. The `date` is missing, so the customer ID ended up in the date column.\n\n**Why `scripts/check.sh` wouldn't have caught it:** the check only reads files for the year in `scripts/check.conf`, which is `year=2025`. Running it now would print OK without looking at `data/2026-01.csv`. So I ran the same field-count check directly on the new file, and that's how I found the row. The other 39 rows are fine.\n\nI first tried a temporary copy of the check script with the year set to 2026, but that was blocked because it needed approval and nobody here can give it.\n\nI removed the copy from `data/`, so the working tree is clean and `inbox/2026-01.csv` is untouched.\n\n**Decisions for you:**\n1. **The missing date for R2601-032:** tell me the date, or fix the inbox file, and I'll add and commit it.\n2. **`check.conf`:** bumping it to `year=2026` would mean 2025 files are no longer checked. It's your call whether to bump it, make the check cover all years, or leave it.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":403,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157,"cache_read_input_tokens":17936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":157,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-25>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T23:56:49.059Z","request_id":"gen-1794700604-OtJxsMCbXCQWqlriEY1B"}
